# Backend address as seen BY THE VITE DEV SERVER (proxy target only, never shipped to
# the client). Only `npm run dev` and `npm run preview` under web/ read it, and only from
# their environment:
# Vite does not load web/.env into its own config, so a value in a copy of this file is
# ignored. Set it on the command line instead:
#   BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:4001 npm run dev
# `npm start` from the repository root serves the built client from the backend itself,
# on one origin, with nothing to configure. Defaults to http://localhost:4000.
